# How the two launchers must reach the other side.
#
# The Windows one needs CRLF line endings: with LF only, cmd.exe can misread
# labels and gotos, and the launcher would skip whole pieces in silence.
# The Mac one needs the opposite, LF: zsh will not run a file whose lines end
# in CRLF, so the app would not start at all.
# Saying it here means it holds on every machine, whatever each person has
# set in their own git.
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.command   text eol=lf

# The program inside Invoice.app is a script too, and it breaks the same way:
# a CRLF after «#!/bin/zsh» and macOS says «bad interpreter» - if it says
# anything at all, because a double-click on a broken app does nothing.
Invoice.app/Contents/MacOS/*   text eol=lf
